  "notes": "{解毒|げどく} refers to the process of neutralizing or removing toxic substances, or to a substance (antidote) that accomplishes this.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {解毒|げどく}{剤|ざい} (antidote)\n- {解毒|げどく}⟦{作用|さよう}→作用：05761_sayou⟧ (detoxifying action)\n- {解毒|げどく}⟦{方法|ほうほう}→方法：03621_houhou⟧ (detoxification method)\n\nThe word is used in both medical and everyday contexts. In medical settings, it often refers to clinical detoxification procedures, while in everyday use it can refer to general concepts of cleansing the body of harmful substances.",
